Evidence (WA, found during k25, confirmed with real Git::Raw in scratch): History/Server _commit_message_for_event builds the generated message from $event->{page}; a rename event has from/to and no page, so a rename without reason is committed as "Renamed page: " (no names).

Fix: the generated message for a rename names both pages ("Renamed page: from -> to"); other events unchanged; a given reason still wins (k25).

Tests: opt-in real Git::Raw (t/51 style): rename without reason -> HEAD message names from and to.

